## BXC Beef Blend substitute

This is a practical AH approximation. Apply it as a **light, even coating**, not a thick crust.

| Ingredient | 6 people / 1.2 kg meat | 8 people / 1.8 kg meat | 10 people / 2.4 kg meat | 12 people / 3 kg meat |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Euroma American Style BBQ | **2¾ tsp** | **4⅛ tsp** | **5½ tsp** | **6⅞ tsp**, about 7 tsp |
| Dark brown sugar | **2¾ tsp** | **4⅛ tsp** | **5½ tsp** | **6⅞ tsp**, about 7 tsp |
| Fine salt | **1¾ tsp** | **2⅝ tsp** | **3½ tsp** | **4⅜ tsp** |
| Instant espresso | **¾ tsp** | **1⅛ tsp** | **1½ tsp** | **1⅞ tsp**, about 2 tsp |

The Euroma blend contains onion, garlic, paprika, smoked paprika, pepper, chilli and herbs but no added salt, which is why salt and sugar are added separately.

Mix everything first. Apply most of it, then stop once the meat is evenly but lightly coated. It is safer to leave a little unused than to oversalt the venison.

